§ `Section 59(4) and section 60 -- seditious intention and its exception`

-- Subsection (4): "Without limiting the generality of the meaning of the expression seditious intention, every one shall be presumed to have a seditious intention who (a) teaches or advocates, or
-- (b) publishes or circulates any writing that advocates, the use, without the authority of law, of force as a means of accomplishing a governmental change within Canada."
-- The presumption does not close the meaning of the term: a case outside it is NOTHING, never JUST FALSE.
-- src:1029 | Seditious intention
-- src:1030 | (4) Without limiting the generality of the meaning of the expression seditious intention, every one shall be presumed to have a seditious intention who
-- src:1031 | (a) teaches or advocates, or
-- src:1032 | (b) publishes or circulates any writing that advocates,
-- src:1033 | the use, without the authority of law, of force as a means of accomplishing a governmental change within Canada.
@ref Criminal Code s 59(4) (seditious intention) (src:1029-1033)
GIVEN `the person teaches or advocates` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person publishes or circulates a writing that advocates` IS A BOOLEAN
      `what is taught or advocated, or advocated in the writing, is the use of force` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the use of force is without the authority of law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the force is a means of accomplishing a governmental change within Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 59(4) the person is presumed to have a seditious intention` MEANS
    IF (`the person teaches or advocates` OR `the person publishes or circulates a writing that advocates`)
        AND `what is taught or advocated, or advocated in the writing, is the use of force`
        AND `the use of force is without the authority of law`
        AND `the force is a means of accomplishing a governmental change within Canada`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "Without limiting the generality of the meaning of the expression seditious intention"

-- Section 60: "Notwithstanding subsection 59(4), no person shall be deemed to have a seditious intention by reason only that he intends, in good faith, (a) to show that Her Majesty has been misled or
-- mistaken in her measures; (b) to point out errors or defects in (i) the government or constitution of Canada or a province, (ii) Parliament or the legislature of a province, or (iii) the administration
-- of justice in Canada; (c) to procure, by lawful means, the alteration of any matter of government in Canada; or (d) to point out, for the purpose of removal, matters that produce or tend to produce
-- feelings of hostility and ill-will between different classes of persons in Canada." A flat negative (JUST FALSE).
-- src:1034 | Exception
-- src:1035 | 60 Notwithstanding subsection 59(4), no person shall be deemed to have a seditious intention by reason only that he intends, in good faith,
-- src:1036 | (a) to show that Her Majesty has been misled or mistaken in her measures;
-- src:1037 | (b) to point out errors or defects in
-- src:1038 | (i) the government or constitution of Canada or a province,
-- src:1039 | (ii) Parliament or the legislature of a province, or
-- src:1040 | (iii) the administration of justice in Canada;
-- src:1041 | (c) to procure, by lawful means, the alteration of any matter of government in Canada; or
-- src:1042 | (d) to point out, for the purpose of removal, matters that produce or tend to produce feelings of hostility and ill-will between different classes of persons in Canada.
@ref Criminal Code s 60 (exception) (src:1034-1042)
DECLARE `s 60 intention` IS ONE OF
    `s 60(a) to show that Her Majesty has been misled or mistaken in her measures`
    `s 60(b)(i) to point out errors or defects in the government or constitution of Canada or a province`
    `s 60(b)(ii) to point out errors or defects in Parliament or the legislature of a province`
    `s 60(b)(iii) to point out errors or defects in the administration of justice in Canada`
    `s 60(c) to procure, by lawful means, the alteration of any matter of government in Canada`
    `s 60(d) to point out, for the purpose of removal, matters that produce or tend to produce feelings of hostility and ill-will between different classes of persons in Canada`
    `s 60 another intention`

@ref Criminal Code s 60 (exception) (src:1034-1042)
GIVEN intention IS A `s 60 intention`
      `the person intends it in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person would be deemed to have a seditious intention by reason only of that intention` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 60 the person is deemed to have a seditious intention` MEANS
    IF intention EQUALS `s 60 another intention` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by reason only that he intends, in good faith, (a) ... (d)"
    ELSE IF `the person intends it in good faith` AND `the person would be deemed to have a seditious intention by reason only of that intention`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no person shall be deemed to have a seditious intention by reason only that he intends, in good faith,"
         ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by reason only" and "in good faith"

-- src:1029 | Seditious intention
-- src:1030 | (4) Without limiting the generality of the meaning of the expression seditious intention, every one shall be presumed to have a seditious intention who
-- src:1031 | (a) teaches or advocates, or
-- src:1032 | (b) publishes or circulates any writing that advocates,
-- src:1033 | the use, without the authority of law, of force as a means of accomplishing a governmental change within Canada.
-- src:1034 | Exception
-- src:1035 | 60 Notwithstanding subsection 59(4), no person shall be deemed to have a seditious intention by reason only that he intends, in good faith,
-- src:1036 | (a) to show that Her Majesty has been misled or mistaken in her measures;
-- src:1037 | (b) to point out errors or defects in
-- src:1038 | (i) the government or constitution of Canada or a province,
-- src:1039 | (ii) Parliament or the legislature of a province, or
-- src:1040 | (iii) the administration of justice in Canada;
-- src:1041 | (c) to procure, by lawful means, the alteration of any matter of government in Canada; or
-- src:1042 | (d) to point out, for the purpose of removal, matters that produce or tend to produce feelings of hostility and ill-will between different classes of persons in Canada.
@ref Criminal Code s 59(4) and s 60 (seditious intention, exception) (src:1029-1042)
GIVEN `the person teaches or advocates` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person publishes or circulates a writing that advocates` IS A BOOLEAN
      `what is taught or advocated, or advocated in the writing, is the use of force` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the use of force is without the authority of law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the force is a means of accomplishing a governmental change within Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      intention IS A `s 60 intention`
      `the person intends it in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person would be deemed to have a seditious intention by reason only of that intention` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 59(4) and s 60 the person has a seditious intention` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 60 the person is deemed to have a seditious intention` intention `the person intends it in good faith` `the person would be deemed to have a seditious intention by reason only of that intention` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Notwithstanding subsection 59(4), no person shall be deemed to have a seditious intention by reason only that he intends, in good faith,"
        IF `s 59(4) the person is presumed to have a seditious intention` `the person teaches or advocates` `the person publishes or circulates a writing that advocates` `what is taught or advocated, or advocated in the writing, is the use of force` `the use of force is without the authority of law` `the force is a means of accomplishing a governmental change within Canada` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "Without limiting the generality of the meaning of the expression seditious intention"

§ `Section 59(1) to (3) -- seditious words, libel and conspiracy`

-- The three definitions say "are", "is": closed definitions (a case that is not within them is JUST FALSE). Whether an intention is a seditious intention is the answer of subsection (4) read
-- with section 60 (`s 59(4) and s 60 the person has a seditious intention`), which may be NOTHING: the term is not closed by the text.
-- src:1023 | Seditious words
-- src:1024 | 59 (1) Seditious words are words that express a seditious intention.
-- src:1025 | Seditious libel
-- src:1026 | (2) A seditious libel is a libel that expresses a seditious intention.
-- src:1027 | Seditious conspiracy
-- src:1028 | (3) A seditious conspiracy is an agreement between two or more persons to carry out a seditious intention.
@ref Criminal Code s 59(1) to (3) (seditious words, seditious libel, seditious conspiracy) (src:1023-1028)
GIVEN `the words express a seditious intention: the answer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 59(1) the words are seditious words` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the words express a seditious intention: the answer`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Seditious words are words that express a seditious intention"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): "seditious intention" is not defined in full

@ref Criminal Code s 59(2) (seditious libel) (src:1023-1028)
GIVEN `it is a libel` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the libel expresses a seditious intention: the answer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 59(2) the libel is a seditious libel` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `it is a libel` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A seditious libel is a libel that expresses a seditious intention"
        IF `the libel expresses a seditious intention: the answer` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the libel expresses a seditious intention: the answer` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A seditious libel is a libel that expresses a seditious intention"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): "seditious intention" is not defined in full

@ref Criminal Code s 59(3) (seditious conspiracy) (src:1023-1028)
GIVEN `the number of persons who are party to the agreement` IS A NUMBER
      `the agreement is to carry out a seditious intention: the answer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 59(3) the agreement is a seditious conspiracy` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the number of persons who are party to the agreement` LESS THAN 2 THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A seditious conspiracy is an agreement between two or more persons"
        IF `the agreement is to carry out a seditious intention: the answer` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the agreement is to carry out a seditious intention: the answer` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A seditious conspiracy is an agreement between two or more persons to carry out a seditious intention"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): "seditious intention" is not defined in full

§ `Section 61 -- Punishment of seditious offences`

-- src:1043 | Punishment of seditious offences
-- src:1044 | 61 Every one who
-- src:1045 | (a) speaks seditious words,
-- src:1046 | (b) publishes a seditious libel, or
-- src:1047 | (c) is a party to a seditious conspiracy,
-- src:1048 | is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding fourteen years.
@ref Criminal Code s 61 (punishment of seditious offences) (src:1043-1048)
DECLARE `s 61 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 61(a) speaks seditious words`
    `s 61(b) publishes a seditious libel`
    `s 61(c) is a party to a seditious conspiracy`
    `s 61 an act that is none of those in paragraphs (a) to (c)`

@ref Criminal Code s 61 (punishment of seditious offences) (src:1043-1048)
GIVEN act IS A `s 61 act`
      `s 59(1) the words are seditious words: the answer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 59(2) the libel is a seditious libel: the answer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 59(3) the agreement is a seditious conspiracy: the answer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 61 the person commits a seditious offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER act
    WHEN `s 61(a) speaks seditious words` THEN `s 59(1) the words are seditious words: the answer`   -- JUST TRUE; JUST FALSE as the definition says no; NOTHING as it leaves open
    WHEN `s 61(b) publishes a seditious libel` THEN `s 59(2) the libel is a seditious libel: the answer`
    WHEN `s 61(c) is a party to a seditious conspiracy` THEN `s 59(3) the agreement is a seditious conspiracy: the answer`
    WHEN `s 61 an act that is none of those in paragraphs (a) to (c)` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "Every one who (a) speaks seditious words, (b) publishes a seditious libel, or (c) is a party to a seditious conspiracy"

@ref Criminal Code s 61 (punishment of seditious offences) (src:1043-1048)
`s 61 the class of the offence` MEANS `an indictable offence`

@ref Criminal Code s 61 (punishment of seditious offences) (src:1043-1048)
`s 61 the punishment` MEANS
    LIST Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `fourteen years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

§ `Section 62 -- Offences in relation to military forces`

-- Subsection (2): "member of a force means a member of (a) the Canadian Forces; or (b) the naval, army or air forces of a state other than Canada that are lawfully present in Canada."
-- "Canadian Forces" is s 2's term: its answer is a seam input (MAYBE BOOLEAN). A "means" definition: outside (a) and (b) the answer is JUST FALSE.
-- src:1054 | Definition of member of a force
-- src:1055 | (2) In this section, member of a force means a member of
-- src:1056 | (a) the Canadian Forces; or
-- src:1057 | (b) the naval, army or air forces of a state other than Canada that are lawfully present in Canada.
@ref Criminal Code s 62(2) (definition of member of a force) (src:1054-1057)
GIVEN `s 2 Canadian Forces: the person is a member of the Canadian Forces` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person is a member of the naval, army or air forces of a state other than Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `those forces are lawfully present in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 62(2) the person is a member of a force` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 2 Canadian Forces: the person is a member of the Canadian Forces` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the person is a member of the naval, army or air forces of a state other than Canada` AND `those forces are lawfully present in Canada` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `s 2 Canadian Forces: the person is a member of the Canadian Forces` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): s 2 "Canadian Forces" leaves the question open
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "member of a force means a member of"

-- src:1049 | Offences in relation to military forces
-- src:1050 | 62 (1) Every person is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than five years or is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction who intentionally
-- src:1051 | (a) interferes with, impairs or influences the loyalty or discipline of a member of a force,
-- src:1052 | (b) publishes, edits, issues, circulates or distributes a writing that advises, counsels or urges insubordination, disloyalty, mutiny or refusal of duty by a member of a force, or
-- src:1053 | (c) advises, counsels, urges or in any manner causes insubordination, disloyalty, mutiny or refusal of duty by a member of a force.
@ref Criminal Code s 62(1) (offences in relation to military forces) (src:1049-1053)
DECLARE `s 62(1) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 62(1)(a) interferes with, impairs or influences the loyalty or discipline of a member of a force`
    `s 62(1)(b) publishes, edits, issues, circulates or distributes a writing that advises, counsels or urges insubordination, disloyalty, mutiny or refusal of duty by a member of a force`
    `s 62(1)(c) advises, counsels, urges or in any manner causes insubordination, disloyalty, mutiny or refusal of duty by a member of a force`
    `s 62(1) an act that is none of those in paragraphs (a) to (c)`

@ref Criminal Code s 62(1) (offences in relation to military forces) (src:1049-1053)
GIVEN act IS A `s 62(1) act`
      `the person acts intentionally` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 62(2) the person is a member of a force: the answer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 62(1) the person commits an offence in relation to a member of a force` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 62(2) the person is a member of a force: the answer` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "member of a force means a member of" (subsection (2))
        IF act EQUALS `s 62(1) an act that is none of those in paragraphs (a) to (c)` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "who intentionally (a) ... (b) ... or (c) ..."
        IF NOT `the person acts intentionally` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "who intentionally"
        IF `s 62(2) the person is a member of a force: the answer` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): s 2 "Canadian Forces" leaves the question open

@ref Criminal Code s 62(1) (punishment) (src:1049-1050)
`s 62(1) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

@ref Criminal Code s 62(1) (punishment) (src:1049-1050)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 62(1) the punishment` MEANS
    LIST (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `five years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`), `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`
